List-Id: Linux and Red Hat on Alpha processors <axp-list.redhat.com>

If you're using the Netscape packages from Red Hat Linux and you've
had Netscape die before displaying a window on startup, here's how to
get Netscape running again:

xprop -remove _MOTIF_DRAG_WINDOW -root

It looks like a bogus window id is causing the problem...

Matt




