> then make bzImage or zImage
> 
> and says and error messages  "no target to rule
> something".

You want "make boot".  That will leave a gzip'ed kernel in
arch/alpha/boot.

(Both the zImage and bzImage targets are x86-specific, while the boot
target is available for all archs.)

> can you help me how will i compile it?
> another thing, what will i choose at alpha system type,
> it is EB164?

The "generic" kernel will work just fine.

