Hi all.  I was in need of some suggestions regarding Linux, so I figured
this was a good place to start.  Here at Finger Lakes Community College we
are running an Alpha Server that currently has OpenVMS  as its operating
system.  We want to replace the OpenVMS OS with the Linux OS.  There are
several reasons for this such as limited support for OpenVMS by
faculty/staff, ect...  Anyways, we were looking for some software products
for Linux, and I was curious as to if anyone had any suggestions for what we
could use.

First of all, we would need a Cobol compiler.  We have one on our OpenVMS
system, and that works pretty good for what we need it for.  But if we move
to Linux, we obviously can't use that anymore.  We have looked at Cobol
compilers for Windows systems, but aren't too impressed with what we have
seen.  So can anyone suggest a good Cobol compiler (doesn't necessarily have
to be free) that could possibly fit our needs?  Mainly it will be used so
that the teachers here can still teach Cobol in their classes.

The other thing I was looking for, is suggestions for a web-based email
package that would be used to handle student email here at the college.  It
would need to be able to handle approximately 3000 - 4000 users or so.  I
know there are a ton of web based email programs out there, the trick is to
find a decent one.  Does anyone have any suggestions as to ones they have
used, good or bad ones, and ones that have support that's backed by a
company?  It would be alright if we had to pay for the software and/or
support for it, as they would like to know here at the college that there
was proper support for it providing there were configuration problems or
other troubles later on down the road.  Or is there an all-in-one package
that will do sending and receiving of email, act as a web server, and also
do the web based email?  As apposed to say...  sendmail / apache / and some
other web based email product that would all have to work together.  Any
suggestions regarding this would be extremely helpful.  Thanks everyone.

-Brian

---------------------------------
Brian A. Miles
Computer Systems Administrator
Finger Lakes Community College 
milesba@flcc.edu




