On Fri, 27 Oct 2000, Brian Miles wrote:

> The other thing I was looking for, is suggestions for a web-based email
> package that would be used to handle student email here at the college.  It
> would need to be able to handle approximately 3000 - 4000 users or so.  I
> know there are a ton of web based email programs out there, the trick is to
> find a decent one.  Does anyone have any suggestions as to ones they have
> used, good or bad ones, and ones that have support that's backed by a
> company?  It would be alright if we had to pay for the software and/or
> support for it, as they would like to know here at the college that there
> was proper support for it providing there were configuration problems or
> other troubles later on down the road.  Or is there an all-in-one package
> that will do sending and receiving of email, act as a web server, and also
> do the web based email?  As apposed to say...  sendmail / apache / and some
> other web based email product that would all have to work together.  Any
> suggestions regarding this would be extremely helpful.  Thanks everyone.

Dunno about the cobol compiler, so I can't help you with that one.  But
there are a whole bunch of web mail applications at http://freshmeat.net.
Most of the better ones require an SQL backend, usually MySQL.
Conveniently, there are binary mysql rpms at ftp.alphalinux.org.

As far as the web mail apps themselves, I've heard good things about IMP.

Mike
