As far as cobol is concerned perhaps you could ask somone at Compaq?  

For web mail interfaces we are using SQwebmail from Inter7.com It's a free
program and inter7 says they support it (We've never needed a support
contract)  It supports SQL backends as well as virtualmail hosts.  The big
thing for me is that it is designed to work with QMAIL and Maildirs.  We
currently use it with about 2500 mail accounts.  With PIII 500 and 256mb
of ram.  It was running on a PII 200 with 128mb of ram no problems.  It
includes a spell checker, universal address books (ldap) and is NOT a
gateway to POP3 for IMAP (It reads users Maildirs directly). I know it
compiles fine on RH 5.2 on alpha (Haven't tested it in on more recent
distro's as we are phasing out our alphas :( ) 

We also use vpopmail from the same inter7.com and run hundreds of domains
and pop accounts through a single userID on another box.  If you don't
want to give users accounts on the mail machine vpopmail plus sqwebmail is
a very good combination (Again designed to work with qmail or any other
mailer that uses Maildir format).

I would suggest using some mail program that uses the Maildir format,
especially if you use NFS anywhere for user homedirs.  

