With regards to your message at 09:43 AM 10/28/00, Olle Hansson. Where you 
stated:
>Hi..
>I have deicded to buy a new network device to my PWS433a
>What budiet card is supported under Digital Unix?
>
>I Know that the digital 2114x chip is supported, but what type of card use 
>that chip?
>
>/Thanks Olle hansson
Just getting a 2114x chip is not enough. The card also has to be 
recognized/support by Tru64.
The genuine DEC/Compaq DE-500 cards work, as do the newer DE-600 if you 
have recent firmware. For some older versions of Tru64 an OS patch is also 
needed.
Other than those models the onboard ethernet on some Intraserver cards such 
as their 4140 and 6110 also works.


