> On Mon, Oct 30, 2000 at 05:38:31PM -0700, Chris Price wrote:
> > 
> > 	Would these 'performance patches' be of any use
> > on older 21064A and 21164A based systems (alphastation400 and
> > XL300/366)?
> 
> You'll see hardly any improvement on EV4/EV45 or EV5/EV56.
> 
> The performance enhancements are due almost entirely to 
> taking advantage
> of architectural features available only on EV6 or later CPUs.
> 
> They are:
> 
> 1. scheduling of instructions specifically for EV6.
> 2. use of instructions available only on EV67 ("cttz", etc).
> 3. use of the "wh64" (write hint) instruction (defined early on,
>    but not implemented until EV6).
> 
