I'm using a VT320 on a DigitalServer 3300 right now (the 1st serial port is
already an MMJ connector... can you tell this was really an AS800? =) )

This 'should' be the right pinout here:
DECconnect DEC-423 MMJ pinout:

    1 Data Terminal Ready (DTR)
    2 Transmit
    3 Transmit Ground
    4 Receive Ground
    5 Receive
    6 Data Set Ready (DSR)

I'll verify this (I have a DEC MMJ->DB9 converter at home that I can trace)

The terminal has to be set to 9600/n/8/1

if you want to use a serial console on the alpha, make sure you have serial
console support in your kernel and then add 'console=ttyS0' to your boot
string

to respawn the getty on the serial port, add this line to your /etc/inittab

S1:2345:respawn:/sbin/mingetty ttyS0 


good luck,
Kurt Ludwig

