Hi Kurt,

Thanks for your reply!


--- Kurt Ludwig <Kurt.Ludwig@alpha-processor.com>
wrote:
> I'm using a VT320 on a DigitalServer 3300 right now
> (the 1st serial port is
> already an MMJ connector... can you tell this was
> really an AS800? =) )

All of our VAXes have MMJ connectors on them.  I wish
they would put MMJs on OEM logic boards (apart from
the SROM) as well :-/

> 
> This 'should' be the right pinout here:
> DECconnect DEC-423 MMJ pinout:
> 
>     1 Data Terminal Ready (DTR)
>     2 Transmit
>     3 Transmit Ground
>     4 Receive Ground
>     5 Receive
>     6 Data Set Ready (DSR)
> 
> I'll verify this (I have a DEC MMJ->DB9 converter at
> home that I can trace)

Okay, thanks in advance!  The pin-to-pin relationship
between the MMJ and DB9 was where my primary confusion
was...

The pin-to-pin diagrams I've seen are not consistent
on three primary points:

1.  Some have MMJs pins 3 & 4 tied together.  This
would make sense since the DB9 only has one signal
ground pin.

2.  Some have no DSR/DTR connection between the MMJ
and DB9.

3.  Some do not appear to be consistent on the tx/rx
lines on the MMJ...

I suppose that your pinout will be correct since your
console apparently works ;-)

> 
> The terminal has to be set to 9600/n/8/1
> 
> if you want to use a serial console on the alpha,
> make sure you have serial
> console support in your kernel and then add
> 'console=ttyS0' to your boot
> string
> 
> to respawn the getty on the serial port, add this
> line to your /etc/inittab
> 
> S1:2345:respawn:/sbin/mingetty ttyS0 

Excellent!  I would never have thought to specify the
console as an argument... man, that would be
frustrating otherwise ;-)

Thanks again,
Rob Parnell



