On Tue, 31 Oct 2000, SteveCraft wrote:

> 
> Has anyone used Arkeia as their backup solution?
> 
> I have my AXP Linux build here, but an NT server on the LAN with the tape
> drive.  Arkeia seems to make something that has an AXP Linux client that
> will talk to an NT server.
> 
> I was originally trying to make a shell script that would make the Linux
> box tar to an FTP site on the NT box and then make NT back that up, but it
> sure is ugly.  It looks like Arkeia has something CLI that I can simply
> cron and let it run.
> 
> Any thoughts?

I've never used Arkeia, but you might also want to look at Amanda. Amanda
is a pretty comprehensive network backup package that uses either gnu tar
or whatever version of dump that's on the machine you're backing up.
It'll also do indexes and has some cool features like allowing you to
have the backup server compress the data, or have each backup target
compress it's own data, or have no software compression at all (for
example if you use the tape drive's hardware compression).

Very nice, especially in a heterogenous environment.  Check it out at
http://www.amanda.org.

Mike
